{"name":"Waterfall","hex":"#3ab0a2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Waterfall","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A stylistic art trend for furniture which was popular in the 1930s and 1940s, featuring wooden surfaces and curved edges prominently in its design.","A barangay of Aurora, Zamboanga del Sur, Philippines."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Waterfall"}],"entries":[{"title":"Waterfall","blocks":[{"text":"A waterfall is any point in a river or stream where water flows over a vertical drop or a series of steep drops. Waterfalls also occur where meltwater drops over the edge \nof a tabular iceberg or ice shelf. Waterfalls can be formed in several ways, but the most common method of formation is that a river courses over a top layer of resistant bedrock before falling onto softer rock, which erodes faster, leading to an increasingly high fall. Waterfalls have been studied for their impact on species living in and around them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Cascada_Dynjandi%2C_Vestfir%C3%B0ir%2C_Islandia%2C_2014-08-14%2C_DD_136-138_HDR.JPG/330px-Cascada_Dynjandi%2C_Vestfir%C3%B0ir%2C_Islandia%2C_2014-08-14%2C_DD_136-138_HDR.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waterfall","wikidata":"Q34038"},{"title":"Waterfall (B.I album)","blocks":[{"text":"Waterfall is the debut studio album, and the second charity album by South Korean rapper, singer, songwriter, record producer and dancer B.I. It was released on June 1, 2021, by IOK Music X 131 Label, and distributed by Dreamus. The album contains 12 songs including the lead single \"Illa Illa\", all written and co-composed by B.I. Waterfall tells a condensed story of B.I's year-and-a-half-long hiatus from his perspective."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2b/B.I_Waterfall_Album_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waterfall_(B.I_album)","wikidata":"Q107291952"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Ulaan_tsutgalan%2C_Mongolia.jpg/500px-Ulaan_tsutgalan%2C_Mongolia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Ulaan_tsutgalan%2C_Mongolia.jpg/1280px-Ulaan_tsutgalan%2C_Mongolia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Ulaan_tsutgalan%2C_Mongolia.jpg/500px-Ulaan_tsutgalan%2C_Mongolia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ulaan tsutgalan in Mongolia During Summer 2023, the background is showing more geological structures formations and farther geological features","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUlaan_tsutgalan%2C_Mongolia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Iceland_Dettifoss_1972-4.jpg/500px-Iceland_Dettifoss_1972-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Iceland_Dettifoss_1972-4.jpg/1280px-Iceland_Dettifoss_1972-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Iceland_Dettifoss_1972-4.jpg/500px-Iceland_Dettifoss_1972-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Dettifoss in Iceland on 31 July 1972","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIceland_Dettifoss_1972-4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/American_Falls_Niagara_Falls_USA_from_Skylon_Tower_on_2002-05-28.png/500px-American_Falls_Niagara_Falls_USA_from_Skylon_Tower_on_2002-05-28.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thum